      "text": "This script takes the value-weighted monthly section of `6_Portfolios_2x3.csv`, which is the first block in the file, and computes SMB as the average of the three small-cap portfolios minus the average of the three big-cap portfolios. The file has several sections (value- and equal-weighted, monthly and annual), so the parser stops at the end of the monthly value-weighted block. Missing codes (-99.99 or -999) become NaN, and any month with a missing portfolio is dropped.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nIN_FILE = \"6_Portfolios_2x3.csv\"\nOUT_FILE = \"output.csv\"\n\nwith open(IN_FILE, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n    lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\ndate_re = re.compile(r\"^\\d{6}$\")\n\n# Locate the \"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\" section\nstart = None\nfor i, l in enumerate(lines):\n    low = l.lower()\n    if \"value weighted\" in low and \"monthly\" in low:\n        start = i\n        break\n\nrows = []\ncollecting = False\nfor l in lines[(start + 1 if start is not None else 0):]:\n    parts = [p.strip() for p in l.split(\",\")]\n    first = parts[0] if parts else \"\"\n    if date_re.match(first) and len(parts) >= 7:\n        collecting = True\n        vals = []\n        for x in parts[1:7]:\n            try:\n                v = float(x)\n            except ValueError:\n                v = np.nan\n            if v <= -99 or np.isnan(v):  # missing codes -99.99 / -999\n                v = np.nan\n            vals.append(v)\n        rows.append([int(first)] + vals)\n    else:\n        if collecting:\n            # end of the monthly value-weighted block\n            break\n        # otherwise still skipping header/preamble lines\n\nif not rows:\n    raise SystemExit(\"No monthly value-weighted data found\")\n\ndf = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\"date\", \"SL\", \"SM\", \"SH\", \"BL\", \"BM\", \"BH\"])\n\n# Ken French 3-factor SMB: average of small portfolios minus average of big portfolios\ndf[\"value\"] = df[[\"SL\", \"SM\", \"SH\"]].mean(axis=1) - df[[\"BL\", \"BM\", \"BH\"]].mean(axis=1)\n\nout = df.loc[df[\"value\"].notna(), [\"date\", \"value\"]].copy()\nout[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\nout.to_csv(OUT_FILE, index=False, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\nprint(f\"Wrote {len(out)} rows to {OUT_FILE}\")\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
